// unattended-upgrades must NOT reboot the node itself. kured does it (changed 2026-11-18).
//
// History: on 2026-07-18 this file turned on Automatic-Reboot at a staggered hour per node
// (wk-1 03:30, wk-2 04:30). Before that, nodes ran old kernels indefinitely and only picked up a
// new one during an unplanned restart. The automatic reboot fixed that, but it never drained
// the node. Pods were killed in place and restarted into stale state on the same node. After
// every wk-2 kernel reboot (Sep-Nov 2026), Argo CD's repo-server crash-looped
// (`/bin/ln: Already exists`), and no deploy happened until someone restarted it by hand.
//
// Now: upgrades still install unattended, and a kernel update still writes
// /var/run/reboot-required. The kured DaemonSet (deploy/platform/kured) watches that file on the
// worker nodes. Inside its 03:00-05:00 window it cordons and drains the node, reboots it, and
// uncordons it. A lock means only one node at a time, so the per-node stagger is no longer
// needed.
//
// ms-1 and the edge node have no kured pod, so their pending reboots stay a manual,
// operator-watched job (deploy/dr/UPGRADE.md).
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot "false";
